WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.600
Plenty of things from the Predator franchise
have become ingrained in the public consciousness

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.900
over the decades, but there's a lot that's
still unknown about these deep space big game

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.339
hunters, and plenty of things we do know that
remain confusing.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:13.980
We're here to help sort it out.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.540
There's a lot we don't know about the Predators.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.840
For example, the word "predator" is just what
earthlings call these monsters.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:20.660
"We took a vote.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:21.800
'Predator's' cooler, right?"

00:00:22.009 --> 00:00:25.680
Their language in the movies appears to be
a collection of clicking noises represented

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.510
through a complex series of dashes in writing,
so we're never quite sure what they prefer

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:30.180
to be called.

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:34.200
That said, the Predator expanded universe
has revealed in the past that they're an alien

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.240
species known as the Yautja, or the Hish-Qu-Ten.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:41.800
According to the lore, that latter name is
"alien" speak for "The People Who Take Territory."

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.360
Whatever you want to call them, there are
a handful of broad traits they share that

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.520
come up throughout each film.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.160
First of all, the race seems to be guided
by a desire to hunt for sport.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.000
Often they'll seek out whatever passes for
the greatest warriors in a given area and

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.320
stalk them as trophy game.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:56.880
"This thing is hunting us.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:58.280
All of us."

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:02.800
They've even been known to pass on human beings
that don't pose an immediate threat or challenge,

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:06.380
hinting that they might be guided by a twisted
sense of honor or sportsmanship.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.460
They also seem to typically hunt in units
of no more than three.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.440
When they arrive at their hunting grounds,
they're ready for combat, with elaborate armor

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:23.310
designed to help them track prey and turn
invisible, and a helmet that allows them to

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:27.560
see heat signatures and other highly specific
filters on the visual spectrum.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:31.420
If you do manage to get through that armor,
you'll be greeted with bright green luminescent

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.800
blood, assuming they don't self-destruct first.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.820
Not much is known about the Predators' place
of origin.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.820
They're advanced enough to travel the galaxy
but they've also shown signs of having a singular

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:43.620
home world with its own distinct culture and
hierarchy.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:47.200
However, none of that is really explained
to any of the human beings that encounter

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.640
the Predators, they're often too busy running
for their lives to swap stories.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:54.660
Instead, humans typically deal with the warrior
class of the Predators, those that are brave

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:57.330
enough to put boots on the ground and collect
human trophies.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:58.420
"He's on safari.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:01:59.740
Lions.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:00.940
The tigers.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.040
The bears.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:03.920
Oh my…"

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.160
"Trophies."

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:10.099
The Predator species has a sort of tribe mentality,
and they're not above having conflicts amongst

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:10.600
themselves.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:14.680
In short, part of what makes the Predators
so scary is the fact that humans don't quite

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:18.560
know where they come from or what exactly
they want other than to hunt them down and

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.030
dispatch them with extreme violence.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:25.529
The first time we see Predators encountering
humanity is in 1987, in the jungles of Central

00:02:25.529 --> 00:02:26.260
America.

00:02:26.529 --> 00:02:30.879
The first Predator film sees U.S. Special
Operations Forces veteran Major Alan "Dutch"

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:34.870
Schaefer lead a group of five highly trained
commandos and an old friend from the CIA on

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:37.420
a daring mission against some guerrilla troops.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.379
On their way to the extraction point, the
group of mercenaries finds itself stalked

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:45.320
by something that picks them off one by one.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:49.280
Despite their training, they are simply no
match for their bigger, stronger, and more

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:50.939
technologically advanced opponent.

00:02:50.939 --> 00:02:54.939
However, the armor starts to crack when Dutch
realizes that the creature seems to be hunting

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.980
for sport, when he sees it ignore an unarmed
female captive.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.300
"Run!

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:01.540
Go!

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.240
Get to da CHOPPA!"

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.620
Dutch also discovers a strategic advantage
in the midst of battle.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:11.769
When he's knocked into the mudbank of a river,
the Predator has a tough time seeing him because

00:03:11.769 --> 00:03:14.640
being covered in cold mud has reduced his
heat signature.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.900
Armed with some camouflage and makeshift traps,
he engages the creature once more.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:28.040
"AAAAAAHHHHHHHHHH!"

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:32.599
Through a series of clever strikes and brute
force, Dutch is able to damage the Predator,

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:37.000
who responds by taking off its mask in an
apparent show of respect for a worthy opponent.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.220
"You're one ugly motherf---er."

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:45.079
Facing off one final time, Dutch manages to
capture the creature in a trap, forcing it

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:48.620
to set off a self-destruct bomb to eliminate
any trace of its failed hunt.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.540
The Predators return years later for 1990's
Predator 2.

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:04.320
After witnessing the heroism of police Lieutenant
Michael R. Harrigan, this new Predator proceeds

00:04:04.329 --> 00:04:06.239
to hunt the cops and robbers in his orbit.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:10.620
Harrigan unknowingly tracks the monster before
encountering Agent Peter Keyes, who informs

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.820
him that the U.S. government is aware of the
extraterrestrial threat.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:16.020
"A f---ing alien!"

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:20.240
Keyes reveals the bout with Dutch in Central
America was only the latest in a string of

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:21.660
encounters in combat zones.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:25.580
After discovering that the Predator feeds
on animal meat, the feds set up a trap for

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:28.810
the Predator at a slaughterhouse, thinking
they have the upper hand by masking their

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:29.580
heat signatures.

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:33.880
However, the Predator switches to a different
view on his helmet and tracks their flashlights.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:37.680
With any advantage they might have had now
kaput, everyone but Harrigan is killed.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:44.760
Eventually, Harrigan chases the Predator to
its ship and engages it in single combat.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:48.639
After he scores a narrow win, several more
Predators uncloak themselves and collect their

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:49.680
dead comrade's body.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:53.860
They present Harrigan with an antique pistol
as a trophy for besting their champion and

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:57.220
allow him to leave the ship unharmed before
they take off in defeat.

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:59.660
This is where things get complicated.

00:04:59.789 --> 00:05:03.940
The same year fans caught a brief glimpse
of a Xenomorph skull in Predator 2, Fox, which

00:05:03.949 --> 00:05:09.270
owned both the Alien and Predator movie franchises,
licensed a series of crossover comic tie-ins

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:12.800
that eventually led to the 2004 film Alien
vs. Predator.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:17.290
Though not well received critically, AvP provides
perhaps the biggest glimpse into the culture

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:19.039
and the purpose of the Predators.

00:05:19.039 --> 00:05:23.540
In the film, a group of scientists led by
industrial tycoon Charles Bishop Weyland discovers

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:27.060
an underground pyramid some 2000 feet beneath
the ice in Norway.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:31.620
Weyland leads the team on an exploratory mission
just as a trio of Predators arrive at the

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:32.680
entrance to the pyramid.

00:05:32.949 --> 00:05:36.539
Through their exploration, they learn that
the Predator species created the Xenomorphs

00:05:36.539 --> 00:05:41.199
from early humans, who had worshiped the invaders
as gods and allowed themselves to be transformed

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:42.440
into the 'ultimate prey'.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:47.660
Every 100 years the Predators return to create
and hunt the human sacrifices-turned-Xenomorphs

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:49.760
in a rite of passage for their species.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:59.700
Two of the trio sent on the 2004 hunt die
quickly, while one manages to eradicate this

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:03.940
century's Xenomorph threat by befriending
a tough-as-nails woman named Alexa Woods.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:08.060
As a slew of Predators that had been surveying
the conflict appear, they too offer her a

00:06:08.069 --> 00:06:12.650
weapon as a trophy for her successful fight
and leave with their fallen comrade, presumably

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:13.680
back to their planet.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:18.419
However, as soon as they leave the dead Predator
alone, a Predator/Xenomorph hybrid emerges

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:22.900
from its chest to terrorize the ship full
of hunters before it even leaves Earth's atmosphere.

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:30.379
Alien vs. Predator was followed by a sequel,
Aliens vs. Predator: Requiem, but there's

00:06:30.379 --> 00:06:34.389
an ongoing debate over whether these films
count as canonical for either franchise.

00:06:34.389 --> 00:06:38.919
When Ridley Scott returned to the Alien franchise
for the prequels Prometheus and Alien: Covenant,

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:42.060
he completely ignored the AvP story of the
Xenomorphs' origins.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:47.460
Aliens vs. Predator: Requiem picks up right
after the events of AvP.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:51.159
With a hybrid onboard that we will refer to
as the "Predalien", the ship from the end

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:53.400
of the previous film crash-lands in Colorado.

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:57.700
A lone survivor sends a signal to the Predator
homeworld warning them that the Xenomorph

00:06:57.700 --> 00:06:58.620
threat persists.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:01.740
One hunter takes it upon himself to go to
Earth and eliminate them.

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:05.880
Unfortunately, the sequel focuses heavily
on the members of the small Colorado town

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:08.060
where the Predator and Predalien have their
conflict.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:12.220
As a result, it doesn't do much to further
the story of the species other than to highlight

00:07:12.229 --> 00:07:16.330
the lengths the Predators will go to in order
to claim victory over the Xenomorphs.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:20.340
The movie's climax sees the Predator facing
off against the Predalien in single combat.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:24.280
Both of them inflict mortal wounds on the
other before the government drops a tactical

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:28.060
nuke on the small town that's now overrun
with aliens, and that's that.

00:07:28.289 --> 00:07:32.040
The film ends with the Predator's plasma blaster
falling into the hands of Weyland's corporate

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:36.270
partner, Yutani, who declares that the world
simply isn't ready for this kind of technology

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:37.820
to be unleashed on human beings.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:43.500
Set days before Halloween in 2018, The Predator
kicks off as a group of soldiers is attacked

00:07:43.509 --> 00:07:46.599
by one of the alien creatures during a mission
on foreign soil.

00:07:46.599 --> 00:07:50.639
U.S. Army Ranger Quinn McKenna manages to
survive and mail himself some of the creature's

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:52.580
armor as proof of its existence.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:56.680
He's debriefed and held captive with a ragtag
group of other soldiers when the Predator

00:07:56.680 --> 00:08:00.580
in question wakes up, and it's definitely
not thrilled to find itself in a government

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:01.080
lab.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:05.380
The Predator quickly escapes, prompting the
soldiers to steal a prison bus and set off

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:07.280
on a mission to retrieve the mailed armor.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:11.240
When they arrive at McKenna's house, they
find his son took the armor to wear as a makeshift

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.240
Halloween costume.

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:15.840
With the Predator on their tail, they track
down the boy and retrieve the armor.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:20.200
Eventually the Predator catches up and forces
them to surrender the items, only to be killed

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:22.140
when a larger Predator suddenly shows up.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:31.380
This new, beastly-looking alien reveals through
a voice translator that the species has stepped

00:08:31.389 --> 00:08:36.270
up its hunting game and is now collecting
DNA of other species to create stronger hybrids.

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:40.580
It's theorized in the film that, because Predators
like a warm climate, global warming is hurling

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:44.160
humanity toward becoming the most attractive
new hot spot for invasion.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:48.620
It also turns out that the original Predator
that attacked McKenna and his gang was delivering

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:53.210
a mysterious package to humanity, and that
it also carried a shocking amount of human

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:54.720
DNA in its own genetic code.

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:58.700
The film ends with McKenna and a group of
scientists realizing that the package the

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:00.480
Predator delivered was left on purpose.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:04.210
Inside is a suit designed to fit on a human
body, one that looks like it's made for the

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:06.360
specific purpose of combating Predators.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:10.800
It doesn't take long for McKenna to call dibs
on the new tech, meaning humanity is now prepared

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:13.820
to fight fire with fire the next time the
Predators come a-hunting.

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:15.700
"That's my new suit, Bubba."

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:21.420
2010's Predators begins when a group of soldiers
from all around the world wake up to find

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:23.060
themselves falling from the sky.

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:26.880
After realizing that they're dealing with
Predators, the group of strangers deduces

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:30.630
that they've been hand-picked as some of Earth's
greatest warriors and brought to some kind

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.020
of intergalactic game preserve.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:33.140
"And we're the game."

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:37.760
Their theory is proven right when they discover
a madman who has survived on the new planet

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:40.500
for what he calls "ten seasons" by scavenging
and hiding.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:44.380
He also reveals that there is a blood feud
between the normal-looking Predators that

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:47.660
fans have seen in previous movies and new,
larger Predators.

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:51.820
It seems that the Predators' DNA splicing
eventually went awry, causing a rift among

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:52.540
the species.

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:56.180
While it seems that the Predators use the
game preserve to sharpen their hunting skills,

00:09:56.190 --> 00:10:00.560
it's also possible that the technology brought
to Earth in The Predator made it so the planet

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:04.080
is no longer a viable hunting ground, which
clearly hasn't stopped them from bringing

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:05.320
the hunt to their own turf.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:09.320
Sadly, although two members of the party defeat
the monsters, they fail in their mission to

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:11.340
get off the planet and back home to safety.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:15.331
As a result, no one on Earth knows about this
new strategy of kidnapping humans to hunt

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:20.140
off-planet, meaning McKenna's cool new suit
may be useless to save humanity after all.

